.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success, partial reads included; also when the reader of stdout goes away
early.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error, such as a filter needing
.B \-\-attrs full
on a scan without it; also a saved scan whose tree
.B scans \-\-check
finds changed since.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown flag, a bad value, a cursor or field the verb
cannot take, two saved scans
.B diff
cannot compare, or what this build or platform cannot do, such as
.B \-\-treemap pixels
without the
.B pixels
feature.
.TP
.B 3
The path, or a saved scan asked for, does not exist.
.TP
.B 4
Permission denied on the root, or unreadable directories under
.BR \-\-strict .
.TP
.B 5
A saved index is corrupt, or was written in an index version this duscope
cannot read.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Ctrl\-C): while the tree is read, by a walk or from the file
.B import
names, or while the scan is saved, which then saves nothing.
